Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:43:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Radio: AM/FM switch, presets, settings at the top right

- An FM / AM switch at the top left. FM tunes 88.0-108.0 MHz in 0.1 MHz
  steps, AM 530-1700 kHz in 10 kHz steps; the tuner's scale is labelled
  for the band (MHz or kHz) and each band remembers its station. Radio
  plugins get am(bool) before freq() on a band change (default: ignored,
  as the RTL-SDR plugin's FM-only streamer can't receive AM).
- Six presets per band under the tuner. Tap to tune to one (an empty one,
  shown as +, saves the current station); hold to save the current station
  over it. The preset that is playing is highlighted.
- The tuner settings gear moves to the tab's top-right corner.
- Dialogs size their body to its minimum size too (plus the scroll area's
  frame), so small bodies no longer get a needless scrollbar.
